WEBVTT

1
01:06:32.202 --> 01:06:35.202
We give you glory, Jesus. We thank you, Lord.

2
01:06:35.202 --> 01:06:38.202
Lord, you are a wonderful God.

3
01:06:38.202 --> 01:06:41.202
We build our lives on you, Lord.

4
01:06:41.202 --> 01:06:45.202
And as Debbie just said, in all sincerity we want to come to you.

5
01:06:45.202 --> 01:06:48.202
And we want to give ourselves to you.

6
01:06:48.202 --> 01:06:54.202
Lord, I pray for us. Lord, I pray that in this month we are in,

7
01:06:54.202 --> 01:06:57.202
towards Easter, towards the cross.

8
01:06:57.202 --> 01:07:02.202
Lord, I want to pray that we come closer and closer with our spirit and our soul and our mind

9
01:07:02.202 --> 01:07:07.202
to the cross and the resurrection of Jesus.

10
01:07:07.202 --> 01:07:10.202
For this is the true nature of the message.

11
01:07:10.202 --> 01:07:13.202
Jesus died for my sins.

12
01:07:13.202 --> 01:07:18.202
And He rose from the dead, so that I can live with Him.

13
01:07:18.202 --> 01:07:20.202
In Jesus' name. Amen.

14
01:07:20.202 --> 01:07:23.202
It's funny what you just said, Debbie.

15
01:07:23.202 --> 01:07:27.202
About that story which is in all four gospels.

16
01:07:27.202 --> 01:07:32.202
I have written down a similar remark here.

17
01:07:32.202 --> 01:07:39.202
I want to talk to you today about the last communion

18
01:07:39.202 --> 01:07:43.202
that Jesus had with his disciples.

19
01:07:43.202 --> 01:07:46.202
If you have your Bible with you, who doesn't?

20
01:07:46.202 --> 01:07:49.202
Who still takes their Bible to church these days?

21
01:07:49.202 --> 01:07:51.202
Give a little wave. Yes, cool.

22
01:07:51.202 --> 01:07:56.202
That's nice, because I'm trying to keep that in the culture of our church

23
01:07:56.202 --> 01:07:59.202
that we don't read the Bible only from the screen,

24
01:07:59.202 --> 01:08:01.202
but that we are really engaged with God's Word.

25
01:08:01.202 --> 01:08:03.202
Your own Bible.

26
01:08:03.202 --> 01:08:07.202
And it doesn't really matter if you are completely used to your own Bible.

27
01:08:07.202 --> 01:08:10.202
It doesn't really matter which translation you are reading from

28
01:08:10.202 --> 01:08:13.202
or if you are reading from an English translation.

29
01:08:13.202 --> 01:08:16.202
Or maybe you are reading a Russian Bible while you are here.

30
01:08:16.202 --> 01:08:18.202
Or a Spanish Bible.

31
01:08:18.202 --> 01:08:20.202
That would be very nice, I think.

32
01:08:20.202 --> 01:08:24.202
But when you read your own Bible, you are one with that Bible.

33
01:08:24.202 --> 01:08:27.202
And that's nice. It flips nicely and then you can read along nicely.

34
01:08:27.202 --> 01:08:32.202
If you have your Bible, please turn with me to Mark chapter 14.

35
01:08:32.202 --> 01:08:34.202
Mark chapter 14.

36
01:08:34.202 --> 01:08:38.202
You have a bookmark, because you have that card there.

37
01:08:38.202 --> 01:08:41.202
But that can't just stay a bookmark.

38
01:08:41.202 --> 01:08:44.202
Because that is of course the challenge we are going to do together.

39
01:08:44.202 --> 01:08:52.202
But also use that card to have Exodus chapter 12 ready.

40
01:08:52.202 --> 01:08:56.202
Don't read it secretly, because that is a spoiler.

41
01:08:58.202 --> 01:09:03.202
Mark chapter 14 and Exodus chapter 12.

42
01:09:04.202 --> 01:09:06.202
I grew up in the church.

43
01:09:08.202 --> 01:09:15.202
I have experienced all the ins and outs for 41 years, all the ins and outs of the church.

44
01:09:15.202 --> 01:09:17.202
I have learned it.

45
01:09:18.202 --> 01:09:21.202
I have always found it wonderful.

46
01:09:21.202 --> 01:09:24.202
I had a period where I...

47
01:09:24.202 --> 01:09:27.202
I have always found it wonderful.

48
01:09:27.202 --> 01:09:30.202
I have always found it wonderful.

49
01:09:30.202 --> 01:09:35.202
I had a period where I imitated a lost son effect.

50
01:09:37.202 --> 01:09:41.202
I wanted to say, you must be obedient to the Bible, but that was not the intention.

51
01:09:42.202 --> 01:09:44.202
But I was indeed a lost son.

52
01:09:44.202 --> 01:09:48.202
But as a child, I really loved Jesus.

53
01:09:48.202 --> 01:09:52.202
I have watched the Jesus film a billion and one times.

54
01:09:54.202 --> 01:09:57.202
Bible stories, wonderful.

55
01:09:57.202 --> 01:09:59.202
Children's Bibles, comic Bibles.

56
01:09:59.202 --> 01:10:01.202
That Bible is well ingrained in me.

57
01:10:01.202 --> 01:10:05.202
But now still the revelation that Jesus is truly Lord of my life.

58
01:10:05.202 --> 01:10:08.202
That came at the age of 25.

59
01:10:08.202 --> 01:10:11.202
And when I came to repentance, I made an agreement with myself.

60
01:10:11.202 --> 01:10:15.202
At least, that is one of my ways of how I want to live my faith.

61
01:10:15.202 --> 01:10:22.202
Everything I do in faith must be a living thing.

62
01:10:22.202 --> 01:10:24.202
Whatever I do, it must be alive.

63
01:10:24.202 --> 01:10:33.202
So when I pray, it must really be a prayer from me to the Father.

64
01:10:33.202 --> 01:10:35.202
I must really be engaged with it.

65
01:10:35.202 --> 01:10:40.202
When I take communion, as has been explained many times, right?

66
01:10:40.202 --> 01:10:46.202
When we take communion, it must not be a ritual.

67
01:10:46.202 --> 01:10:50.202
But we must know what we are doing.

68
01:10:51.202 --> 01:10:57.202
If you don't know what you are doing, and you come and hop, everyone gets a piece of bread, hop hop hop.

69
01:10:57.202 --> 01:11:01.202
Then it ultimately becomes an empty tradition.

70
01:11:01.202 --> 01:11:10.202
While communion must be anything but an empty tradition.

71
01:11:10.202 --> 01:11:17.202
The whole Bible speaks about this situation.

72
01:11:17.202 --> 01:11:19.202
The whole Bible looks forward to it.

73
01:11:20.202 --> 01:11:24.202
The Last Supper and everything surrounding it can be found.

74
01:11:24.202 --> 01:11:28.202
Certainly in the four gospels, as Debbie just said.

75
01:11:28.202 --> 01:11:30.202
And what she just said is very important.

76
01:11:30.202 --> 01:11:39.202
When all four gospels explain something, it is so important that you cannot overlook it.

77
01:11:39.202 --> 01:11:45.202
That is the most important thing, because if one of the evangelists says, well, that doesn't have to be.

78
01:11:45.202 --> 01:11:52.202
Then you can still interpret, okay, great, what does this evangelist mean by that, oh nice.

79
01:11:52.202 --> 01:11:58.202
But if all four gospels talk about it, then it's okay, focus, because this is of essential importance.

80
01:11:58.202 --> 01:12:01.202
John is actually doing his own thing a bit.

81
01:12:01.202 --> 01:12:09.202
So the last communion can be found in Matthew chapter 26, Mark chapter 14, which we will read shortly.

82
01:12:09.202 --> 01:12:11.202
Luke chapter 22.

83
01:12:11.202 --> 01:12:13.202
And John does a bit of his own thing.

84
01:12:13.202 --> 01:12:17.202
Because you know, John is really a very different kind of gospel.

85
01:12:17.202 --> 01:12:22.202
Matthew, Mark, and Luke are the three copied gospels.

86
01:12:22.202 --> 01:12:28.202
The copied, the derived gospel, we call the synoptic gospels.

87
01:12:28.202 --> 01:12:32.202
And that means, they have simply been taken synchronously from each other.

88
01:12:32.202 --> 01:12:36.202
And John is totally busy with something else.

89
01:12:36.202 --> 01:12:42.202
So what is stated in Matthew, Mark, and Luke is not stated in John.

90
01:12:42.202 --> 01:12:47.202
John has his own version in John chapter 6 and in John chapter 17.

91
01:12:47.202 --> 01:12:50.202
If you want to take notes about that, you can study it.

92
01:12:50.202 --> 01:12:57.202
In John chapter 6, Jesus teaches that you must eat his body and drink his blood.

93
01:12:57.202 --> 01:13:01.202
And many people think to themselves, wow, you know.

94
01:13:01.202 --> 01:13:08.202
And in John chapter 17, he is, just like in Matthew, Mark, and Luke, sitting with his friends.

95
01:13:08.202 --> 01:13:15.202
And you see that the whole setting is the same as Matthew, Mark, and Luke's last communion.

96
01:13:15.202 --> 01:13:20.202
Only in that moment, Jesus does not break the bread and distribute it and say, now you may drink the wine.

97
01:13:20.202 --> 01:13:25.202
But he offers a very intense, long prayer.

98
01:13:25.202 --> 01:13:27.202
But they overlap.

99
01:13:27.202 --> 01:13:34.202
So all four gospels and still, when you look at what all this means.

100
01:13:34.202 --> 01:13:37.202
And that is why we are going to take a look at it together.

101
01:13:37.202 --> 01:13:41.202
This is the whole Bible that you see standing here.

102
01:13:41.202 --> 01:13:44.202
This is the entire Bible and we are going to read this together.

103
01:13:44.202 --> 01:13:51.202
And how wonderful, Exodus speaks about it, Genesis speaks about it.

104
01:13:51.202 --> 01:13:54.202
I don't know if you know what typology is.

105
01:13:54.202 --> 01:14:09.202
But as soon as humanity sinned in Genesis chapter 3, God prepares clothing from an animal that had to be slain to cover the sin of humanity.

106
01:14:09.202 --> 01:14:13.202
This is a typology, it doesn't literally say that it was the lamb.

107
01:14:13.202 --> 01:14:19.202
But there is already an immediate kind of prophetic outlook on what Jesus has done for us.

108
01:14:19.202 --> 01:14:27.202
But you see it in Genesis. You see how Melchizedek and Abraham share the evening meal together.

109
01:14:27.202 --> 01:14:36.202
You see it in Exodus. You see that Paul in Corinth speaks about it to say listen, we need to do this neatly and carefully.

110
01:14:36.202 --> 01:14:46.202
You see it in the letter to the Hebrews. So you see the theme coming back everywhere in the Bible of what we are going to celebrate during Easter.

111
01:14:47.202 --> 01:14:57.202
In other words, we cannot afford to just approach it as a piece of bread, a small cup on the side and that's it.

112
01:14:57.202 --> 01:15:00.202
It is far too deep for that. Let's read it together.

113
01:15:00.202 --> 01:15:02.202
Mark chapter 14.

114
01:15:30.202 --> 01:15:36.202
There you will encounter a man carrying a jar of water.

115
01:15:36.202 --> 01:15:42.202
This is a divine appointment. Check this.

116
01:15:42.202 --> 01:15:54.202
Suppose Jesus had said go to the city, you will enter the gate, third tree on the right, there is a carpenter making furniture.

117
01:15:54.202 --> 01:16:00.202
You should knock there. Then it would be a specific assignment to an existing shop or craftsman.

118
01:16:00.202 --> 01:16:09.202
But Jesus does something very special here. He says go to the city and you will meet a man walking with a jar.

119
01:16:09.202 --> 01:16:15.202
This must be more than coincidence. This must be a divine appointment.

120
01:16:15.202 --> 01:16:17.202
Are you following me or not?

121
01:16:17.202 --> 01:16:26.202
So you see that the man who walks 24/7, knowing that the disciples are coming.

122
01:16:26.202 --> 01:16:30.202
Oh yes, okay, I agreed with Jesus, so for the next three days I will walk here with a jar.

123
01:16:30.202 --> 01:16:35.202
So that when they come, the disciples will say, ah you are the man where...

124
01:16:35.202 --> 01:16:39.202
He doesn't wear a t-shirt all day saying hello, I'm that guy.

125
01:16:39.202 --> 01:16:42.202
No, he walks with a jar. It's something heavy.

126
01:16:42.202 --> 01:16:48.202
First of all, it was something for either slaves or definitely for women. It was actually a woman's task.

127
01:16:48.202 --> 01:16:54.202
So what you see here is really something very special.

128
01:16:54.202 --> 01:17:05.202
I hope in my life, I hope for your life, that you experience divine appointments with God.

129
01:17:05.202 --> 01:17:09.202
Because you understand what I mean by divine appointments.

130
01:17:10.202 --> 01:17:13.202
Divine means divine encounters.

131
01:17:13.202 --> 01:17:20.202
So I hope for you that you experience many divine encounters in your life.

132
01:17:20.202 --> 01:17:29.202
Because these are those powerful moments that you will always remember, God is real.

133
01:17:29.202 --> 01:17:38.202
He lives. He is the one who is not just a theoretical God from paper, he is a living God.

134
01:17:38.202 --> 01:17:44.202
And so when Jesus says to his disciples, go into the city, at least that's how I read the Bible.

135
01:17:44.202 --> 01:17:50.202
Go into the city and there you will meet a man carrying a jar of water.

136
01:17:50.202 --> 01:17:56.202
Okay, if you are one of the disciples, having been with Jesus for three years now,

137
01:17:56.202 --> 01:18:02.202
you start to gain trust that if Jesus says that, then it might actually come true.

138
01:18:02.202 --> 01:18:07.202
But with the command itself, you might think to yourself, what?

139
01:18:08.202 --> 01:18:13.202
At another moment, Jesus says, go to the city, go into the city,

140
01:18:13.202 --> 01:18:19.202
and there is a donkey or a young colt and you just need to take it.

141
01:18:19.202 --> 01:18:21.202
That is strange.

142
01:18:21.202 --> 01:18:29.202
That is the same as saying, go to Lommel, in the center there is a car, you just have to take that car.

143
01:18:29.202 --> 01:18:33.202
That is the same level. That is strange.

144
01:18:33.202 --> 01:18:39.202
We think very simply of the old days, oh yes, that must have been possible in that time.

145
01:18:39.202 --> 01:18:45.202
Such a young foal, a colt, a foal or a donkey, who knows what it was, or a crossbreed of it,

146
01:18:45.202 --> 01:18:49.202
was very valuable.

147
01:18:49.202 --> 01:18:53.202
So to just take that and then walk away, and then Jesus says,

148
01:18:53.202 --> 01:18:55.202
and if someone says, hey, what are you going to do with that?

149
01:18:55.202 --> 01:18:59.202
Because if you just take a car, then eventually someone will also say, hey, what are you going to do with that?

150
01:18:59.202 --> 01:19:02.202
Then you say, the Lord needs it.

151
01:19:02.202 --> 01:19:10.202
Okay, the disciples of Jesus really had a hard time.

152
01:19:10.202 --> 01:19:12.202
Right?

153
01:19:12.202 --> 01:19:16.202
But we are still disciples of Jesus.

154
01:19:16.202 --> 01:19:22.202
We are still, 2000 years later, still disciples of Jesus.

155
01:19:22.202 --> 01:19:26.202
And we, on a daily basis, on a daily level,

156
01:19:26.202 --> 01:19:31.202
encounter things in our lives that make you think to yourself, but how then?

157
01:19:32.202 --> 01:19:33.202
Right?

158
01:19:33.202 --> 01:19:37.202
And that’s why what Debbie just said, so powerful, that connection.

159
01:19:37.202 --> 01:19:39.202
Thanks, sis.

160
01:19:39.202 --> 01:19:43.202
That’s why you need to have trust in Jesus.

161
01:19:43.202 --> 01:19:48.202
And not on the task, or the logic of the task.

162
01:19:48.202 --> 01:19:53.202
God loves to put the logic of the task under immense pressure.

163
01:19:53.202 --> 01:19:57.202
So that we trust in Him, and not our logic.

164
01:19:57.202 --> 01:19:59.202
Let's move on.

165
01:19:59.202 --> 01:20:04.202
Follow Him and go into the house where He enters.

166
01:20:04.202 --> 01:20:08.202
Say to the Lord of that house, so that is not the same person.

167
01:20:08.202 --> 01:20:14.202
The master asks where He can eat the Passover with His disciples.

168
01:20:14.202 --> 01:20:17.202
The man will show you a large upper room.

169
01:20:17.202 --> 01:20:23.202
This is probably the same upper room where the Holy Spirit descends.

170
01:20:23.202 --> 01:20:27.202
We call this the Upper Room, the upper room.

171
01:20:27.202 --> 01:20:30.202
The man will show you a large upper room.

172
01:20:30.202 --> 01:20:32.202
There is everything we need.

173
01:20:32.202 --> 01:20:35.202
Prepare the meal for us there.

174
01:20:35.202 --> 01:20:37.202
The two disciples departed.

175
01:20:37.202 --> 01:20:42.202
They came into the city and everything went as Jesus had said.

176
01:20:42.202 --> 01:20:44.202
Can we say amen to that?

177
01:20:44.202 --> 01:20:45.202
I find it so beautiful.

178
01:20:45.202 --> 01:20:49.202
And everything went as Jesus had said.

179
01:20:49.202 --> 01:20:53.202
That is why I want to have trust in Him.

180
01:20:53.202 --> 01:20:56.202
I do not want to have trust in myself.

181
01:20:56.202 --> 01:21:02.202
My situations do not turn out as I would have liked.

182
01:21:02.202 --> 01:21:05.202
I already have trouble planning my entire day.

183
01:21:05.202 --> 01:21:07.202
If you know me, everyone says amen.

184
01:21:07.202 --> 01:21:08.202
Please do not do that.

185
01:21:08.202 --> 01:21:11.202
But I already have trouble planning my day.

186
01:21:11.202 --> 01:21:18.202
God knows exactly how my life can work out best.

187
01:21:18.202 --> 01:21:20.202
I want to trust in Him.

188
01:21:20.202 --> 01:21:26.202
For here it says they came into the city and everything went as Jesus had said.

189
01:21:26.202 --> 01:21:27.202
Thank you, Lord.

190
01:21:27.202 --> 01:21:29.202
They prepared the Passover meal.

191
01:21:29.202 --> 01:21:34.202
When evening had come, He came together with the twelve disciples.

192
01:21:34.202 --> 01:21:37.202
During the meal, Jesus said, listen carefully.

193
01:21:37.202 --> 01:21:42.202
I tell you that one of you will betray me here.

194
01:21:42.202 --> 01:21:46.202
One of you who eats with me.

195
01:21:46.202 --> 01:21:48.202
They were very sad about this.

196
01:21:48.202 --> 01:21:51.202
They asked Him one by one, is it I?

197
01:21:51.202 --> 01:21:59.202
He answered, it is one of the twelve who dips bread with me in the same bowl.

198
01:21:59.202 --> 01:22:09.202
The Son of Man will die in the way that has already been written in the books about Him.

199
01:22:10.202 --> 01:22:12.202
Why is this important?

200
01:22:12.202 --> 01:22:19.202
Because Jesus is fulfilling something that the whole Bible looks forward to.

201
01:22:19.202 --> 01:22:23.202
God is not random.

202
01:22:23.202 --> 01:22:26.202
God is not a God of chance.

203
01:22:26.202 --> 01:22:31.202
God knew from the beginning of creation exactly what He was going to do.

204
01:22:31.202 --> 01:22:38.202
Man will die in the way that has already been written in the books about Him.

205
01:22:38.202 --> 01:22:42.202
But it will go badly for the man who has betrayed Him.

206
01:22:42.202 --> 01:22:47.202
It would have been better for him if he had not been born.

207
01:22:47.202 --> 01:22:50.202
While they were eating, Jesus took bread.

208
01:22:50.202 --> 01:22:52.202
He blessed it.

209
01:22:52.202 --> 01:22:55.202
Broke it into pieces and gave it to them.

210
01:22:55.202 --> 01:22:58.202
He said, take this and eat it.

211
01:22:58.202 --> 01:23:00.202
It is my body.

212
01:23:00.202 --> 01:23:03.202
Then He took a cup of wine.

213
01:23:03.202 --> 01:23:05.202
Here you see them standing.

214
01:23:05.202 --> 01:23:09.202
He thanked God for it and gave it to the disciples.

215
01:23:09.202 --> 01:23:11.202
They drank from it one by one.

216
01:23:11.202 --> 01:23:19.202
And He said to them, this wine is my blood with which God establishes a new covenant with the people.

217
01:23:19.202 --> 01:23:24.202
That blood is poured out for many people.

218
01:23:24.202 --> 01:23:28.202
I tell you that from now on, and I want us to focus on this here.

219
01:23:29.202 --> 01:23:33.202
I tell you that from now on I will not drink wine anymore.

220
01:23:33.202 --> 01:23:38.202
Until I drink new wine in the kingdom of God.

221
01:23:38.202 --> 01:23:43.202
After they had sung the thanksgiving songs, they went to the Mount of Olives.

222
01:23:47.202 --> 01:23:51.202
What is so important about the last communion?

223
01:23:51.202 --> 01:23:53.202
What does Jesus fulfill with this?

224
01:23:53.202 --> 01:23:57.202
It is important as a church that we go through these things.

225
01:23:57.202 --> 01:24:00.202
Because in the church there are people who can dream this.

226
01:24:00.202 --> 01:24:03.202
But in the church there are also many people who do not know this beforehand.

227
01:24:03.202 --> 01:24:08.202
And that is why we are going to spend some more time in Exodus chapter 12 together.

228
01:24:08.202 --> 01:24:11.202
Come with me to Exodus chapter 12.

229
01:24:11.202 --> 01:24:16.202
You must understand that there is 1500 years between this.

230
01:24:18.202 --> 01:24:20.202
1500 years, that is a long time.

231
01:24:20.202 --> 01:24:29.202
1500 years ago, God began something here that Jesus fulfills at that moment.

232
01:24:31.202 --> 01:24:36.202
I am thinking about whether I should do this now or later.

233
01:24:37.202 --> 01:24:40.202
A question came to me this week.

234
01:24:40.202 --> 01:24:42.202
Just a side street.

235
01:24:43.202 --> 01:24:45.202
But follow me on this one.

236
01:24:46.202 --> 01:24:55.202
Regularly, a question comes to me about Israel and about the Jewish faith.

237
01:24:55.202 --> 01:25:02.202
We pray as a church for Israel, for the repentance of Israel.

238
01:25:02.202 --> 01:25:12.202
And we stand with Israel because we want to see our older brother come to repentance.

239
01:25:13.202 --> 01:25:18.202
And very often or regularly I receive questions about this.

240
01:25:18.202 --> 01:25:20.202
How should I pray for that?

241
01:25:20.202 --> 01:25:22.202
What should I think about that?

242
01:25:22.202 --> 01:25:25.202
I see all kinds of things happening in the news.

243
01:25:25.202 --> 01:25:27.202
How do we deal with that?

244
01:25:27.202 --> 01:25:29.202
One thing I want to say.

245
01:25:29.202 --> 01:25:33.202
God has not given up on Israel.

246
01:25:34.202 --> 01:25:38.202
Jesus does not set Israel aside.

247
01:25:39.202 --> 01:25:45.202
Jesus fulfills what is happening in Israel.

248
01:25:45.202 --> 01:25:48.202
And it is important for us to understand.

249
01:25:48.202 --> 01:25:54.202
For what you see happening here is that Jesus is continuing something.

250
01:25:54.202 --> 01:25:59.202
Jesus is carrying on with something from Israel.

251
01:25:59.202 --> 01:26:03.202
So even if God had said goodbye to Israel.

252
01:26:03.202 --> 01:26:07.202
Even if he had said, Israel has been so wrong.

253
01:26:07.202 --> 01:26:10.202
And they have nailed the Son of God to a cross.

254
01:26:10.202 --> 01:26:12.202
And they have killed him.

255
01:26:12.202 --> 01:26:14.202
And he could not lay his head on a stone.

256
01:26:14.202 --> 01:26:19.202
And he could no longer be with Israel.

257
01:26:19.202 --> 01:26:21.202
And he curses the fig tree.

258
01:26:21.202 --> 01:26:22.202
You all know that moment.

259
01:26:22.202 --> 01:26:24.202
He curses the fig tree.

260
01:26:24.202 --> 01:26:28.202
And with that, he says, just like with the temple that we talked about last week.

261
01:26:28.202 --> 01:26:30.202
He goes through the temple with a whip.

262
01:26:30.202 --> 01:26:32.202
And he becomes very angry with Israel.

263
01:26:32.202 --> 01:26:38.202
Doesn't that mean that Jesus is saying he is done with Israel?

264
01:26:38.202 --> 01:26:40.202
By no means.

265
01:26:40.202 --> 01:26:43.202
Suppose he were done with Israel.

266
01:26:43.202 --> 01:26:46.202
We would have something very strange in the love of God.

267
01:26:46.202 --> 01:26:51.202
Then we would have a few thousand years of love for Israel.

268
01:26:51.202 --> 01:26:53.202
And blessing Israel.

269
01:26:53.202 --> 01:26:55.202
And showing Israel that he is for Israel.

270
01:26:55.202 --> 01:26:57.202
And all the nations were afraid.

271
01:26:57.202 --> 01:27:00.202
For everyone knew that God was for Israel.

272
01:27:00.202 --> 01:27:02.202
And love for Israel, love for Israel.

273
01:27:02.202 --> 01:27:04.202
But Israel is just like you and me sinful.

274
01:27:04.202 --> 01:27:06.202
And we disappoint God.

275
01:27:06.202 --> 01:27:07.202
And we are dealing with that.

276
01:27:07.202 --> 01:27:09.202
And then he says, suppose that.

277
01:27:09.202 --> 01:27:11.202
Suppose God says at that moment.

278
01:27:11.202 --> 01:27:13.202
And now I am completely done with Israel.

279
01:27:13.202 --> 01:27:15.202
Then that means.

280
01:27:15.202 --> 01:27:18.202
That we are heading towards a time from the New Testament.

281
01:27:18.202 --> 01:27:20.202
That God loves the whole world.

282
01:27:20.202 --> 01:27:22.202
Except for Israel.

283
01:27:22.202 --> 01:27:24.202
Makes no sense.

284
01:27:26.202 --> 01:27:29.202
Why do we call Jesus Messiah?

285
01:27:29.202 --> 01:27:32.202
Messiah is a Jewish word.

286
01:27:32.202 --> 01:27:34.202
If we want to do away with that.

287
01:27:34.202 --> 01:27:36.202
Then we will only call him Jesus Christ.

288
01:27:36.202 --> 01:27:39.202
And there are very large groups that only say Jesus Christ.

289
01:27:39.202 --> 01:27:41.202
He is Jesus the Messiah.

290
01:27:41.202 --> 01:27:43.202
Can I get an amen on that?

291
01:27:43.202 --> 01:27:45.202
And also the Passover.

292
01:27:45.202 --> 01:27:48.202
And now I come back to what we are doing.

293
01:27:48.202 --> 01:27:52.202
Also the Passover does not exclude Jesus.

294
01:27:52.202 --> 01:27:55.202
But he actually takes it over.

295
01:27:55.202 --> 01:27:58.202
To tell it to the people.

296
01:27:58.202 --> 01:28:01.202
So Jesus indeed.

297
01:28:01.202 --> 01:28:03.202
Is 'continue' a good word Marco?

298
01:28:03.202 --> 01:28:05.202
Yes, right?

299
01:28:05.202 --> 01:28:07.202
So Jesus continues.

300
01:28:07.202 --> 01:28:09.202
What Israel is.

301
01:28:09.202 --> 01:28:11.202
He continues with it.

302
01:28:11.202 --> 01:28:17.202
To give a short answer to what Jesus then says no more.

303
01:28:17.202 --> 01:28:19.202
Is simply.

304
01:28:19.202 --> 01:28:21.202
That fig tree symbolizes.

305
01:28:21.202 --> 01:28:24.202
Something had to bear fruit.

306
01:28:24.202 --> 01:28:28.202
The only thing Jesus dismisses at that moment.

307
01:28:28.202 --> 01:28:31.202
Is the religious system.

308
01:28:31.202 --> 01:28:37.202
By which man could come closer to God through blood sacrifices.

309
01:28:37.202 --> 01:28:39.202
Of that Jesus says.

310
01:28:39.202 --> 01:28:41.202
This no longer bears fruit.

311
01:28:41.202 --> 01:28:44.202
What they are doing here in the temple.

312
01:28:44.202 --> 01:28:47.202
With all those blood sacrifices and grain offerings and this offering and that offering.

313
01:28:47.202 --> 01:28:50.202
And observing it this way.

314
01:28:50.202 --> 01:28:52.202
And doing it that way.

315
01:28:52.202 --> 01:28:55.202
Apparently, that no longer brought people closer to God.

316
01:28:55.202 --> 01:28:56.202
And Jesus says.

317
01:28:56.202 --> 01:28:58.202
Now I am completely done with it.

318
01:28:58.202 --> 01:29:01.202
The prophets in the Old Testament were also done with it.

319
01:29:01.202 --> 01:29:03.202
And also said.

320
01:29:03.202 --> 01:29:05.202
I have no need for blood sacrifices at all.

321
01:29:05.202 --> 01:29:07.202
I want you hard.

322
01:29:07.202 --> 01:29:09.202
I want you to be hard.

323
01:29:09.202 --> 01:29:11.202
And Jesus the ultimate prophet.

324
01:29:11.202 --> 01:29:13.202
The Son of God.

325
01:29:13.202 --> 01:29:16.202
The lamb that was slain before the foundation of the world.

326
01:29:16.202 --> 01:29:20.202
Says to the religious system of Judaism.

327
01:29:20.202 --> 01:29:22.202
This no longer bears fruit.

328
01:29:22.202 --> 01:29:24.202
And pay close attention.

329
01:29:24.202 --> 01:29:26.202
The moment he says.

330
01:29:26.202 --> 01:29:27.202
This no longer bears fruit.

331
01:29:27.202 --> 01:29:29.202
He does not dismiss it.

332
01:29:29.202 --> 01:29:30.202
But he says.

333
01:29:30.202 --> 01:29:33.202
This time is now fulfilled.

334
01:29:33.202 --> 01:29:36.202
This is now over.

335
01:29:36.202 --> 01:29:39.202
This is now complete.

336
01:29:39.202 --> 01:29:42.202
Why is it important to say this?

337
01:29:42.202 --> 01:29:44.202
Suppose he says.

338
01:29:44.202 --> 01:29:45.202
This is garbage.

339
01:29:45.202 --> 01:29:47.202
This is wrong.

340
01:29:47.202 --> 01:29:50.202
Then he says about the law of Moses that it is wrong.

341
01:29:50.202 --> 01:29:52.202
But that was not it.

342
01:29:52.202 --> 01:29:55.202
The law of Moses came from Jesus Himself.

343
01:29:55.202 --> 01:29:58.202
The law of Moses came from God.

344
01:29:58.202 --> 01:30:00.202
But he says.

345
01:30:00.202 --> 01:30:02.202
This is now fulfilled.

346
01:30:02.202 --> 01:30:05.202
What does Jesus say when He is hanging on the cross?

347
01:30:05.202 --> 01:30:07.202
It is finished.

348
01:30:07.202 --> 01:30:09.202
He does not say on the cross.

349
01:30:09.202 --> 01:30:11.202
What was that bad.

350
01:30:11.202 --> 01:30:13.202
He says rightly.

351
01:30:13.202 --> 01:30:15.202
What this has been.

352
01:30:15.202 --> 01:30:16.202
Jesus.

353
01:30:16.202 --> 01:30:18.202
The ultimate.

354
01:30:18.202 --> 01:30:19.202
Easter.

355
01:30:19.202 --> 01:30:20.202
Lamb.

356
01:30:20.202 --> 01:30:21.202
Offering.

357
01:30:21.202 --> 01:30:22.202
Is He.

358
01:30:22.202 --> 01:30:25.202
So that we no longer have to come to Him with offerings.

359
01:30:25.202 --> 01:30:28.202
But we must go to Jesus as a person.

360
01:30:28.202 --> 01:30:29.202
Amen.

361
01:30:29.202 --> 01:30:31.202
So let us read Exodus chapter 12.

362
01:30:31.202 --> 01:30:33.202
In all love for Israel.

363
01:30:33.202 --> 01:30:36.202
We must therefore pray for Israel.

364
01:30:36.202 --> 01:30:38.202
That they may come to repentance.

365
01:30:38.202 --> 01:30:39.202
To King Jesus.

366
01:30:39.202 --> 01:30:42.202
They are indeed part of our faith.

367
01:30:42.202 --> 01:30:43.202
Hallelujah.

368
01:30:43.202 --> 01:30:45.202
Exodus chapter 12.

369
01:30:47.202 --> 01:30:50.202
The Lord said to Moses and Aaron.

370
01:30:52.202 --> 01:30:55.202
Pay close attention to these words. Verse 2.

371
01:30:55.202 --> 01:30:57.202
This month.

372
01:30:57.202 --> 01:31:00.202
Shall henceforth be for you.

373
01:31:01.202 --> 01:31:03.202
The most important month.

374
01:31:04.202 --> 01:31:08.202
It shall be the first month of the year.

375
01:31:08.202 --> 01:31:10.202
How beautiful is that.

376
01:31:10.202 --> 01:31:12.202
What Jesus does.

377
01:31:12.202 --> 01:31:14.202
Is so important.

378
01:31:14.202 --> 01:31:17.202
That God in the Old Testament says.

379
01:31:17.202 --> 01:31:20.202
This is the most important thing that happens.

380
01:31:20.202 --> 01:31:23.202
The Bible is never accidental in what it does.

381
01:31:23.202 --> 01:31:29.202
The Bible has always been written with very attentive intent.

382
01:31:29.202 --> 01:31:33.202
What is written is exactly what the Bible means.

383
01:31:33.202 --> 01:31:35.202
So when God says.

384
01:31:35.202 --> 01:31:37.202
The Lord said to Moses and Aaron.

385
01:31:37.202 --> 01:31:39.202
This month shall henceforth be for you.

386
01:31:39.202 --> 01:31:42.202
The most important month.

387
01:31:42.202 --> 01:31:45.202
It shall be the first month of the year.

388
01:31:45.202 --> 01:31:48.202
Say to the whole people of Israel.

389
01:31:48.202 --> 01:31:50.202
On the tenth day of this month.

390
01:31:50.202 --> 01:31:52.202
Everyone must take a lamb.

391
01:31:52.202 --> 01:31:54.202
That is King Jesus.

392
01:31:54.202 --> 01:31:56.202
Choose it from the flock.

393
01:31:56.202 --> 01:31:59.202
One lamb per household.

394
01:31:59.202 --> 01:32:02.202
But if someone's household is too small for that.

395
01:32:02.202 --> 01:32:05.202
He must share with a neighbor.

396
01:32:05.202 --> 01:32:10.202
There must be enough meat for all the people of two households.

397
01:32:10.202 --> 01:32:12.202
When selecting the animal.

398
01:32:12.202 --> 01:32:16.202
You must take into account how much everyone eats.

399
01:32:16.202 --> 01:32:18.202
Here it comes.

400
01:32:18.202 --> 01:32:21.202
It must be a healthy male animal.

401
01:32:21.202 --> 01:32:23.202
From one year old.

402
01:32:23.202 --> 01:32:24.202
Primetime.

403
01:32:24.202 --> 01:32:25.202
The very best.

404
01:32:25.202 --> 01:32:27.202
It must not be a little goat either.

405
01:32:27.202 --> 01:32:30.202
It can also be a little goat that is one year old.

406
01:32:30.202 --> 01:32:32.202
Here it comes.

407
01:32:32.202 --> 01:32:36.202
There must be absolutely nothing wrong with it.

408
01:32:38.202 --> 01:32:40.202
You see the symbolism, right?

409
01:32:40.202 --> 01:32:45.202
You must keep it until the fourteenth day of this month.

410
01:32:45.202 --> 01:32:48.202
So you must keep that animal.

411
01:32:48.202 --> 01:32:49.202
To have bees.

412
01:32:49.202 --> 01:32:50.202
To love.

413
01:32:50.202 --> 01:32:54.202
Then all the Israelites must slaughter those animals.

414
01:32:54.202 --> 01:32:56.202
When evening comes.

415
01:32:56.202 --> 01:32:59.202
After that, you must take the blood.

416
01:32:59.202 --> 01:33:00.202
There we have the blood.

417
01:33:00.202 --> 01:33:04.202
Of the animals to smear on the doorposts.

418
01:33:04.202 --> 01:33:09.202
Around the doors of the houses where you eat the animals.

419
01:33:09.202 --> 01:33:11.202
That same day.

420
01:33:11.202 --> 01:33:12.202
That same night.

421
01:33:12.202 --> 01:33:14.202
You must eat the meat.

422
01:33:14.202 --> 01:33:18.202
Eat it roasted with bread made of dough.

423
01:33:18.202 --> 01:33:20.202
Without yeast.

424
01:33:20.202 --> 01:33:22.202
And with bitter herbs.

425
01:33:22.202 --> 01:33:25.202
You may not eat the meat boiled or raw.

426
01:33:25.202 --> 01:33:29.202
You may only eat it roasted.

427
01:33:29.202 --> 01:33:35.202
You must eat the whole animal with the head, the legs, and the entrails.

428
01:33:35.202 --> 01:33:39.202
You may not keep any of it until the next day.

429
01:33:39.202 --> 01:33:42.202
What remains of it, you must burn.

430
01:33:42.202 --> 01:33:45.202
You must eat it in haste.

431
01:33:45.202 --> 01:33:51.202
Be ready to leave while eating, with shoes on and a staff in your hand.

432
01:33:51.202 --> 01:33:56.202
For it is, and here comes the word, the Passover offering.

433
01:33:56.202 --> 01:34:01.202
For Passover, pascha, means to pass by.

434
01:34:01.202 --> 01:34:03.202
For the Lord.

435
01:34:03.202 --> 01:34:08.202
For I will go through Egypt tonight and strike down all the oldest sons and all the firstborn animals.

436
01:34:08.202 --> 01:34:11.202
I will bring judgment on all the gods of Egypt.

437
01:34:11.202 --> 01:34:13.202
I am the Lord.

438
01:34:13.202 --> 01:34:16.202
The blood on your houses is a sign.

439
01:34:16.202 --> 01:34:20.202
When I see the blood on a house, I will pass over that house.

440
01:34:20.202 --> 01:34:25.202
Thus, no one among you will die when I strike Egypt.

441
01:34:25.202 --> 01:34:29.202
This day, and here we have the sandwich, here we have the end.

442
01:34:29.202 --> 01:34:33.202
This day must henceforth be a feast for you.

443
01:34:33.202 --> 01:34:36.202
A feast for me, the Lord.

444
01:34:36.202 --> 01:34:42.202
All your families after you must celebrate this feast forever.

445
01:34:42.202 --> 01:34:45.202
I want to say the word forever once more.

446
01:34:45.202 --> 01:34:49.202
What does forever mean in the mindset of God?

447
01:34:49.202 --> 01:34:52.202
Forever means forever.

448
01:34:52.202 --> 01:34:55.202
Forever means this never stops.

449
01:34:55.202 --> 01:34:59.202
Forever means not until the cross and not beyond.

450
01:34:59.202 --> 01:35:02.202
Forever means forever.

451
01:35:02.202 --> 01:35:10.202
In the book of Revelation, the last book, you also see that the Lamb is celebrated.

452
01:35:10.202 --> 01:35:13.202
And the Lamb is recognizable.

453
01:35:13.202 --> 01:35:16.202
So it is forever.

454
01:35:16.202 --> 01:35:19.202
The similarities that we see here,

455
01:35:19.202 --> 01:35:22.202
and I want to present them in the last few minutes we have together,

456
01:35:22.202 --> 01:35:24.202
so that when we celebrate communion together shortly,

457
01:35:24.202 --> 01:35:27.202
we understand what the similarities are.

458
01:35:27.202 --> 01:35:30.202
There are many, but I want to share a few with you.

459
01:35:30.202 --> 01:35:34.202
The unleavened bread was a feast that Jesus celebrates in Mark chapter 14.

460
01:35:34.202 --> 01:35:40.202


461
01:35:40.202 --> 01:35:44.202
And in Exodus chapter 12 we see the agreement there.

462
01:35:44.202 --> 01:35:47.202
Why did such bread have to be, it probably didn't look like this,

463
01:35:47.202 --> 01:35:51.202
it looked a bit like a durum for example,

464
01:35:51.202 --> 01:35:56.202
probably a bit larger, it was baked quickly,

465
01:35:56.202 --> 01:35:59.202
but why did everything have to be quick?

466
01:35:59.202 --> 01:36:03.202
Firstly, the speed at which it had to be prepared,

467
01:36:03.202 --> 01:36:09.202
means the speed you need to come out of Egypt,

468
01:36:09.202 --> 01:36:14.202
out of your sinful life, to repentance and be saved,

469
01:36:14.202 --> 01:36:16.202
in the name of Jesus.

470
01:36:16.202 --> 01:36:18.202
You should not wait until next week.

471
01:36:18.202 --> 01:36:21.202
You should not wait and say, just a moment,

472
01:36:21.202 --> 01:36:24.202
I want to come to repentance, but I first need to clean this up,

473
01:36:24.202 --> 01:36:26.202
I shouldn't really look at that anymore,

474
01:36:26.202 --> 01:36:28.202
I shouldn't really be doing that anymore,

475
01:36:28.202 --> 01:36:30.202
I shouldn't really be associating with those people anymore,

476
01:36:30.202 --> 01:36:31.202
and then I will come to Jesus.

477
01:36:31.202 --> 01:36:35.202
No, says God, you must come to repentance now, there is urgency.

478
01:36:35.202 --> 01:36:38.202
All the things you do that keep you away from the love of God,

479
01:36:38.202 --> 01:36:40.202
do it now.

480
01:36:40.202 --> 01:36:45.202
Just imagine, everyone who knows the story of Exodus,

481
01:36:45.202 --> 01:36:52.202
so the people of Israel were in Egypt for 400 years in slavery,

482
01:36:52.202 --> 01:36:56.202
and so Egypt symbolizes for your life and mine,

483
01:36:56.202 --> 01:37:01.202
our lives that we had in slavery before we knew Jesus.

484
01:37:01.202 --> 01:37:06.202
Addiction, being under the slavery of sin.

485
01:37:06.202 --> 01:37:12.202
And so Egypt and our current lives have a great resemblance.

486
01:37:12.202 --> 01:37:16.202
And how strange would it be, if you have the people of Israel,

487
01:37:16.202 --> 01:37:20.202
who have been in slavery for 400 years,

488
01:37:20.202 --> 01:37:22.202
and then finally through Moses,

489
01:37:22.202 --> 01:37:29.202
God brings Israel out of Egypt, out of slavery, into freedom.

490
01:37:29.202 --> 01:37:34.202
How strange would it be, if there is someone who thinks to themselves,

491
01:37:34.202 --> 01:37:37.202
I still need to get used to that.

492
01:37:37.202 --> 01:37:41.202
The whole people go, then they all go together,

493
01:37:41.202 --> 01:37:45.202
but I just need a little while, I'll come later.

494
01:37:45.202 --> 01:37:48.202
Pharaoh changes his mind, becomes hard,

495
01:37:48.202 --> 01:37:53.202
comes with his army, everyone goes crazy again in Egypt,

496
01:37:53.202 --> 01:37:56.202
Egypt is angry, and then there is one Israeli who thinks,

497
01:37:56.202 --> 01:38:00.202
yes no, I find that strange.

498
01:38:00.202 --> 01:38:03.202
No, there is urgency.

499
01:38:03.202 --> 01:38:06.202
Just to my life, because I want to talk about this.

500
01:38:06.202 --> 01:38:10.202
There is urgency in the salvation of my life.

501
01:38:10.202 --> 01:38:14.202
There is urgency in the salvation of your life.

502
01:38:14.202 --> 01:38:17.202
I speak to some people in the audience,

503
01:38:17.202 --> 01:38:20.202
come to Jesus, don't wait for that.

504
01:38:20.202 --> 01:38:22.202
There is urgency.

505
01:38:22.202 --> 01:38:26.202
Tomorrow is not a better day than today.

506
01:38:26.202 --> 01:38:29.202
Today could be your last day.

507
01:38:29.202 --> 01:38:32.202
Today is the day of salvation, says the Lord.

508
01:38:32.202 --> 01:38:34.202
Bring it to the Lord.

509
01:38:34.202 --> 01:38:39.202
That was a reason why God said it must be unleavened.

510
01:38:39.202 --> 01:38:42.202
No time to wait until everything is on the journey.

511
01:38:42.202 --> 01:38:46.202
No time to wait to see how slowly you can eat the lamb.

512
01:38:46.202 --> 01:38:52.202
It had to be done with your sandals on, staff in hand, there is urgency.

513
01:38:52.202 --> 01:38:57.202
For today the Lord brings salvation in your life.

514
01:38:57.202 --> 01:39:01.202
The other reason why this bread had to be unleavened,

515
01:39:01.202 --> 01:39:05.202
is because leaven represents sin in the Bible.

516
01:39:05.202 --> 01:39:07.202
It is a symbolism about sin.

517
01:39:07.202 --> 01:39:10.202
And so this bread had to be perfect without leaven.

518
01:39:10.202 --> 01:39:12.202
Leaven rises.

519
01:39:12.202 --> 01:39:14.202
Sin rises in your life.

520
01:39:14.202 --> 01:39:16.202
It shows itself.

521
01:39:16.202 --> 01:39:21.202
If you are sinful, you can't help it, it will eventually come out.

522
01:39:21.202 --> 01:39:26.202
Sooner or later, your sinful nature will take its toll and it will come to the surface.

523
01:39:26.202 --> 01:39:29.202
Anger comes out, aggression comes out,

524
01:39:29.202 --> 01:39:32.202
uncleanness comes out, occultism comes out.

525
01:39:32.202 --> 01:39:36.202
It is the sin that puffs itself up in your life.

526
01:39:36.202 --> 01:39:39.202
But Jesus was pure.

527
01:39:39.202 --> 01:39:42.202
Jesus was without leaven.

528
01:39:42.202 --> 01:39:45.202
Jesus is perfect.

529
01:39:45.202 --> 01:39:48.202
Glory to the name of Jesus.

530
01:39:48.202 --> 01:39:56.202
And that is why you see in both Exodus, prophetically, 1500 years earlier,

531
01:39:56.202 --> 01:40:01.202
that Jesus is the fulfillment of what happened 1500 years before.

532
01:40:01.202 --> 01:40:07.202
I find Jesus so amazing, that I would rather say about the Exodus.

533
01:40:07.202 --> 01:40:10.202
Try to understand what I am saying.

534
01:40:10.202 --> 01:40:13.202
In Exodus, they receive all those commands.

535
01:40:13.202 --> 01:40:17.202
Then I would rather think, why all that symbolism, why?

536
01:40:17.202 --> 01:40:21.202
I would find it difficult 1500 years before that.

537
01:40:21.202 --> 01:40:24.202
Then they are set free and then they sought it must be this way.

538
01:40:24.202 --> 01:40:27.202
It must be perfect this way. It must be perfect this way.

539
01:40:27.202 --> 01:40:33.202
And you must smear the blood of the lamb on the doorposts of your door.

540
01:40:33.202 --> 01:40:37.202
What? Right?

541
01:40:37.202 --> 01:40:42.202
But Jesus makes sense of it all.

542
01:40:42.202 --> 01:40:48.202
Jesus is, ah, by His blood I have been set free.

543
01:40:48.202 --> 01:40:51.202
Ah, wait a moment.

544
01:40:51.202 --> 01:40:58.202
Then, when God saw the blood on the doorposts, He passed over.

545
01:40:58.202 --> 01:41:03.202
And He would not judge you for the sin you have committed.

546
01:41:03.202 --> 01:41:10.202
Small note, it was not necessarily Satan who passed by the doors.

547
01:41:10.202 --> 01:41:14.202
It was God Himself who judges.

548
01:41:14.202 --> 01:41:21.202
The state of the English of death, there is nothing in that it was Satan.

549
01:41:21.202 --> 01:41:25.202
We often say that death and Satan go together.

550
01:41:25.202 --> 01:41:29.202
And I understand that we think this, but it is not what the Bible says.

551
01:41:29.202 --> 01:41:33.202
Satan was another angel. Satan was an accuser.

552
01:41:33.202 --> 01:41:37.202
Satan was an adversary, someone who stands opposite.

553
01:41:37.202 --> 01:41:43.202
But that God says in Exodus chapter 12, I will pass over this night.

554
01:41:43.202 --> 01:41:50.202
And I will kill everyone who lives in sin, unless the blood of the lamb is upon you.

555
01:41:50.202 --> 01:41:52.202
This is the act of God.

556
01:41:52.202 --> 01:41:57.202
God will judge this world.

557
01:41:57.202 --> 01:42:01.202
God will judge this world, unless.

558
01:42:01.202 --> 01:42:07.202
Unless we are covered by the blood of the lamb. Amen.

559
01:42:07.202 --> 01:42:12.202
Another parallel that is important to see is of course

560
01:42:13.202 --> 01:42:18.202
the wine. And I have deliberately placed four glasses here.

561
01:42:18.202 --> 01:42:23.202
You read in Mark, you read that Jesus says,

562
01:42:23.202 --> 01:42:28.202
I tell you that from now on I will not drink wine anymore.

563
01:42:28.202 --> 01:42:32.202
Until I ultimately am in the kingdom of God.

564
01:42:32.202 --> 01:42:35.202
And I don't know about the people who have ever held the Seder meal,

565
01:42:35.202 --> 01:42:39.202
give a wave if you have ever done the Seder meal.

566
01:42:39.202 --> 01:42:46.202
Good. So we celebrate, as a church we celebrate the bread and the wine.

567
01:42:46.202 --> 01:42:52.202
Why? Because Jesus says that we must continue with the bread and the wine.

568
01:42:52.202 --> 01:42:59.202
Jesus does not necessarily say that you must continue to do the Seder meal.

569
01:42:59.202 --> 01:43:02.202
I personally find it beautiful symbolism.

570
01:43:02.202 --> 01:43:06.202
I myself do it regularly with my wife during Easter.

571
01:43:06.202 --> 01:43:11.202
I don't see that it is not allowed. I also don't see that it is required.

572
01:43:11.202 --> 01:43:15.202
I see that Jesus says, do this forever.

573
01:43:15.202 --> 01:43:21.202
But in that Seder meal there are wonderfully beautiful things from which you can learn.

574
01:43:21.202 --> 01:43:24.202
And the focus that I want to talk about for a moment,

575
01:43:24.202 --> 01:43:30.202
is that during the Seder meal you have to go through a number of glasses of wine as a family.

576
01:43:30.202 --> 01:43:35.202
And I just think that it is the Holy Spirit.

577
01:43:35.202 --> 01:43:39.202
Because every time I stand before that last glass of wine,

578
01:43:39.202 --> 01:43:43.202
and it is very symbolically placed on that table, and you have to look at it,

579
01:43:43.202 --> 01:43:48.202
and then Jesus says in Mark chapter 14,

580
01:43:48.202 --> 01:43:52.202
I will never drink of this wine again,

581
01:43:52.202 --> 01:43:55.202
until I drink it again in my kingdom.

582
01:43:55.202 --> 01:44:00.202
So I see something that has been done in Christ,

583
01:44:00.202 --> 01:44:04.202
but which we are still waiting for in expectation.

584
01:44:05.202 --> 01:44:09.202
A fulfillment of time in which it is not yet complete.

585
01:44:09.202 --> 01:44:14.202
A fulfillment of time in which we are still waiting in hope in Jesus Christ,

586
01:44:14.202 --> 01:44:19.202
that the work He has begun in me will continue.

587
01:44:19.202 --> 01:44:25.202
And when He returns and prepares everything in the full glory of who He is,

588
01:44:25.202 --> 01:44:33.202
we will together have the heavenly meal and celebrate what Jesus has done for us.

589
01:44:34.202 --> 01:44:40.202
I find it so nice that I always want to think about what communion is,

590
01:44:40.202 --> 01:44:46.202
what am I actually celebrating, and I want to keep holding on to the comparisons.

591
01:44:46.202 --> 01:44:50.202
I had written down a few more things, but time is up and I want to ask Rudy,

592
01:44:50.202 --> 01:44:53.202
if we can go ahead and distribute communion.

593
01:44:53.202 --> 01:44:55.202
Maybe the band can come back on stage.

594
01:44:55.202 --> 01:44:57.202
But here is one more important thing.

595
01:44:57.202 --> 01:45:08.202
Egypt symbolizes who we were in Christ. Maybe we can stand up.

596
01:45:19.202 --> 01:45:23.202
Yes Rudy, you may go ahead and distribute the bread and the wine.

597
01:45:24.202 --> 01:45:30.202
Egypt of the Old Testament symbolizes who I was before I knew Jesus.

598
01:45:30.202 --> 01:45:36.202
Egypt symbolizes the sin that was over my life,

599
01:45:36.202 --> 01:45:42.202
and it symbolizes that I was not yet in the salvation of God.

600
01:45:42.202 --> 01:45:49.202
Fifteen hundred years later, Jesus celebrates the Passover meal, the Passover,

601
01:45:49.202 --> 01:45:54.202
that I can celebrate together with Jesus, when we break the bread and when we drink the wine,

602
01:45:54.202 --> 01:45:59.202
we can celebrate that sin no longer has power over me.

603
01:45:59.202 --> 01:46:01.202
Can I get an amen on that?

604
01:46:01.202 --> 01:46:10.202
Sin no longer has control over me, but I have been set free by the blood of Jesus and by his body.

605
01:46:11.202 --> 01:46:16.202
And so every time, and I want to keep saying this every time,

606
01:46:16.202 --> 01:46:25.202
when I take the bread, dear church, if you already have the bread in your hands, you can think about your old life.

607
01:46:25.202 --> 01:46:34.202
Maybe you can close your eyes and think about the things, I understand that the trays are still going around,

608
01:46:34.202 --> 01:46:39.202
that we need to do a few logistical things to hold the bread and the wine.

609
01:46:39.202 --> 01:46:45.202
But as soon as you have it in your hands, the bread and the wine, I want to ask you to focus on Jesus.

610
01:46:59.202 --> 01:47:02.202
I want to take this seriously in my own life, people.

611
01:47:02.202 --> 01:47:05.202
I want to keep dealing with this seriously.

612
01:47:05.202 --> 01:47:09.202
I want to realize how sinful my sinful life was.

613
01:47:13.202 --> 01:47:20.202
I want to ask all of us to engage in self-reflection about who you were without Jesus.

614
01:47:20.202 --> 01:47:24.202
And it is always best if you close your eyes.

615
01:47:25.202 --> 01:47:30.202
Because it is your life and your sinfulness.

616
01:47:30.202 --> 01:47:35.202
And when I talk about myself, I just know that I was lost without God.

617
01:47:35.202 --> 01:47:37.202
I was lost without God.

618
01:47:39.202 --> 01:47:45.202
And what we read in Egypt, in the natural from so many thousands of years ago,

619
01:47:45.202 --> 01:47:50.202
is who we were ourselves, without what Jesus has done for us.

620
01:47:52.202 --> 01:47:56.202
I want to ask the Holy Spirit to inspire our hearts.

621
01:47:56.202 --> 01:47:59.202
That moment when Jesus says, this is my body.

622
01:48:02.202 --> 01:48:07.202
And I am broken in place of you.

623
01:48:08.202 --> 01:48:12.202
You do not have to pay for the sin that you have committed.

624
01:48:13.202 --> 01:48:15.202
But I do that, says Jesus.

625
01:48:16.202 --> 01:48:21.202
And as we read in Exodus, that a lamb, that a woman,

626
01:48:22.202 --> 01:48:27.202
And as we read in Exodus, that a lamb must be perfect,

627
01:48:27.202 --> 01:48:31.202
that a bread must be broken perfectly.

628
01:48:32.202 --> 01:48:38.202
In the same way, Jesus went to a cross for your sin.

629
01:48:40.202 --> 01:48:43.202
Holy Spirit, I want to ask you to show everyone in this room

630
01:48:45.202 --> 01:48:49.202
that you are a truly slain lamb.

631
01:48:49.202 --> 01:48:51.202
This is your idea, God.

632
01:48:52.202 --> 01:48:54.202
This is what you have done, for me personally.

633
01:48:54.202 --> 01:48:58.202
Lord, I want to ask you to bless us all,

634
01:49:00.202 --> 01:49:03.202
that as we take the bread and the wine in self-reflection shortly,

635
01:49:03.202 --> 01:49:07.202
while the band is going to sing for us shortly.

636
01:49:07.202 --> 01:49:10.202
You can sit down, you can kneel, you can stand,

637
01:49:10.202 --> 01:49:15.202
but I want to encourage us as a church to be in self-reflection

638
01:49:15.202 --> 01:49:19.202
and in devotion towards Jesus.

639
01:49:19.202 --> 01:49:22.202
That we will give our hearts to Him.

640
01:49:22.202 --> 01:49:25.202


641
01:49:25.202 --> 01:49:28.202
That we will say, Jesus, I need you.

642
01:49:28.202 --> 01:49:33.202
I recognize you as the unleavened bread, I recognize you as sinless.

643
01:49:33.202 --> 01:49:37.202
I recognize you as the lamb that was slain for my sins.

644
01:49:39.202 --> 01:49:41.202
Jesus, I need you.

645
01:49:41.202 --> 01:49:44.202
Lord, I need your blood in my life,

646
01:49:44.202 --> 01:49:49.202
so that the judgment may pass over me.

647
01:49:49.202 --> 01:49:52.202
That I am protected under the blood of Jesus.

648
01:49:54.202 --> 01:49:57.202
Lord, I want to take the bread and the wine together with my brothers and sisters in this room,

649
01:49:57.202 --> 01:50:01.202
for the forgiveness of our sins.

650
01:50:01.202 --> 01:50:04.202
Because we recognize you as without sin.

651
01:50:14.202 --> 01:50:19.202
Church, we may now take the bread and the wine in reflection to Jesus.

